UDCPR-2020
Regulation (hereinafter referred to as "the said regulation") has been approved and is in force from 03.12.2020;
and whereby, in accordance with Regulation No. 1.9 (v) of the said regulation, there is a provision regarding the issuance of orders by the Government in relation to the matters/questions raised in connection with the application of various provisions of the said regulation;
and whereby, the Government has issued guidance to the concerned persons from time to time in accordance with the said provision;
and whereby, the Government has received representations from Amaravati Municipal Corporation and other some organisations regarding the implementation of the provisions of Regulation No. 3.4.1 (i) and 3.5.1 of the said regulation in connection with the difficulties arising in the implementation thereof;
and whereby, considering the said various representations and in the interest of the public, it is necessary to clarify the provisions of the said regulation in order to ensure effective implementation of the said regulation, and the Government has formed the opinion that it is necessary to review such provisions and issue clarification thereof in accordance with Regulation No. 1.9 (v) of the said regulation;
now, therefore, the following explanatory notes are issued in accordance with Regulation No. 3.4.1 (i) and Regulation No. 3.5.1 of the said regulation —
